    "updated_at": "2022-04-25T07:55:59Z",
    "body": "Essentially creating a PR for https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/tree/master/dom/traversal to cover this behavior. That's the repository we use for tests covering the standard.\r\n\r\nAlso, all non-number return values seem to be treated as FILTER_SKIP, rather than coerced. That means that `acceptNode()` has to be amended to return `any` instead of `unsigned short`. And it seems that if the value is a number, `Math.floor()` is applied to it.\r\n\r\nHowever, according to https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/webidl/NodeFilter.webidl#32 Firefox does have the \"accurate\" Web IDL for this. @petervanderbeken are we simply not enforcing that as required (see https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1075#issuecomment-1106410304)? Makes me wonder if there's a larger issue here or maybe I'm just missing something.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
