    "updated_at": "2022-04-25T08:55:58Z",
    "body": "Ah good. It still seems worth creating some tests for the exceptional cases, e.g., `7`, `1n`, or `{ valueOf: () => { throw 1 } }`, across the various method calls to see they indeed end up being treated as a result that is not explicitly handled (when they don't result in throwing). But there's no problem with the specification here after all.",
